<title>COTE D'IVOIRE: ABB seen building Ivory Coast power plant.</title>
<headline>ABB seen building Ivory Coast power plant.</headline>
<dateline>ABIDJAN 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss-Swedish ABB AG has presented the most competitive bid for building a third thermal power plant for Ivory Coast's commercial capital Abidjan, the National Office of Technical Studies and Development said.</p>
<p>ABB proposed an investment of 165 billion CFA francs ($284.5 million) for a 420 megawatt plant, to go on stream in January 1999.</p>
<p>A statement said ABB proposed to produce energy at 7.3 CFA francs per kilowatt hour, compared to 9.52 CFA in the nearest rival bid from U.S. firm AES Corp.</p>
<p>The statement said negotiations would now take place on the details of the project.</p>
<p>Apart from AES, Belgium's Tractebel and U.S. Enron Corp also bid for the project, but their bids did not meet the conditions, the statement said.</p>
<p>($=580CFA)</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom +225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
